  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher systemic US–China tension raises market perceptions of elevated probability of naval confrontations, sanctions or secondary effects that could disrupt Gulf exports, which traders price as an increased oil risk premium.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_rivalry</data>
